// What the world has written down: pages of the Wikimedia sister projects (Wikibooks, Wikivoyage,
// Wikiquote), read as sections of lists. Where to look is derived, not listed: a word whose
// Wikidata item has a page in a namespace of a sister project ("recipe" is Cookbook:Recipes on
// Wikibooks) says that things of that kind are written there, and "how" asks for steps, which are
// written at Wikibooks. Pages are CC BY-SA and are said with where they came from. Written by
// scripts/pack.mjs from sources/pages (edit those, not this).
Requires(Basic(), Pursue())

// A page read from a site: its title, and each section that holds a list, in order.
Concept(Page(), IsA(Result()))

Concept(Section(), IsA(Data()))

// "How do you bake a cake" asks for the steps to do it.
Concept(Steps(), IsA(Category()), WrittenAt(Wikibooks()))

Concept(How(), Asks(Steps()))

// Where a kind of thing is written: the site that holds it.
Concept(WrittenAt(), IsA(Relation()))

Concept(Wikibooks(), Site("https://en.wikibooks.org"))

Concept(Site(), IsA(Relation()))
